Given a quantile summary $Q(\sD) = (S, 	dr^+, 	dr^-, 	dw)$ defined in Definition~ef{def:sketch}, the domain of $	dr^+$, $	dr^-$ and $	dw$ were defined only in $S$. We extend the definition of these functions to $\sX ightarrow \Rplus$ as follows \ 
oindent When $y < x_1$:  egin{equation} 	dr^-(y) = 0, \  	dr^+(y) = 0,\   	dw(y) = 0 \end{equation} 
oindent When $y > x_k$:  egin{equation} 	dr^-(y) = 	dr^+(x_k), \  	dr^+(y) = 	dr^+(x_k),\   	dw(y) = 0 \end{equation} 
oindent When $y \in (x_i, x_{i+1})$ for some $i$:  egin{equation}  egin{split} 	dr^-(y)& =	dr^-(x_i)+	dw(x_i), \ 	dr^+(y)& = 	dr^+(x_{i+1}) - 	dw(x_{i+1}),\   	dw(y)& = 0 \end{split} \end{equation}
